From c225239c9069b600b2d5a3339dc6b29ff10b9bd3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:32:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] soc: apple: capture explicit inherited AOP buffer ranges
 early

AFK 0x89 buffers have per-session physical addresses and may contain a
ring at an offset. Add immutable ring_pa/ring_pa_size lists so an iOS
probe's exact buffer can be captured before a broad sweep reuses RAM.

Capture up to four 64 KiB ranges at postcore, then again after one second.
Use fixed BSS snapshots and page-confined nofault linear-map reads only
after proving System RAM, valid PFNs and a mapped non-no-map range.
Admit mapped reservations, quarantine faults across targets and samples,
and hide partial failed copies. Exclude snapshot and stack pages and
warn when supplied buffers occupy Linux allocator RAM. Do not reserve,
pin, remap, write or maintain caches on the inherited source.

Expose frozen prefix/nonzero-line dumps, offset header matches, range
metadata and byte changes in root-only ring_pa debugfs. PA mode blocks
the active and wrapper paths even for malformed lists. Preserve the
existing broad-scan and reserved IIO contracts.

Signed-off-by: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
